// Hand-curated position availability (positions_race_eras) for cases the
// source data cannot evidence.
//
// tools/import-bbl only asserts availability where it has positive evidence a
// position was played -- a config override, star-player status, or a recorded
// player use in a matching era. Genuine availability the source data cannot
// show is restored here from the rulebook rosters.
//
// This file lives in 002-initial-cleanup, never in 001, and that is load
// bearing: many of the position references below use the "<raceName>:
// <positionName>" Name external id that NameExternalIdService.forPosition
// builds, and that id is only created by tools/import-bbl's position
// importer. Curating before the importers would create an orphan position
// row under that Name id on a fresh database; when BBL later upserts the
// same real position, supplying both its own numeric external id (already
// resolved to a different, earlier-created row) and that same Name id (now
// resolved to the orphan), the two ids point at different rows and the
// upsert throws PositionUpsertConflictError. Curating after ensures BBL has
// already established that position's identity, so these references resolve
// to the correct existing row instead of racing to create a duplicate.
//
// positions_race_eras is keyed per ERA, not per rules set. "First era" and
// "First Stunty Leeg era" each span CRP, CRP+ and BB2016 together, so one row
// covers all three for those eras.
//
// Each entry re-states the position's curated `name` verbatim, because the
// manual importer renames existing rows -- a mismatched name would rename the
// position rather than leave it alone. `isStarPlayer` is likewise re-stated
// (false, for every entry below -- none of these are star players), since on a
// fresh database this batch creates the row and positions.is_star_player is
// NOT NULL.
//
// Restoration set: every position with a curated CRP `position_rules_sets`
// entry in 002-initial-cleanup/position-characteristics.json5 is
// positive rulebook evidence that position was available to its race under
// First era (which spans CRP, CRP+ and BB2016). The same is true, under First
// Stunty Leeg era (which also spans BB2016, CRP and CRP+), for every
// Stunty-Leeg-handbook-sourced position curated there.
//
// Source importers set a position's name only when they create the row, so
// only the manual batches ever rename a position (003-reset-curated-names
// only restates the curated names), and this batch is applied after
// 001-initial-seed. This file and 001-initial-seed/races-and-positions.json5
// must therefore carry the same name for every position they share: a
// different spelling in either file would rename the row back and forth on
// every import. Each entry's `name` equals the name races-and-positions.json5
// gives the same row, and curated-data.spec.ts enforces it for every shared
// Name id.
{
  externalSystems: [
    { name: 'Name', category: 'bookkeeping' },
    { name: 'tloeg.bbleague.se', category: 'imported_data_source' },
  ],
  positions: [
